top:            hbm_weight_tiler
function:       burst-read INT8 weight tiles from an HBM AXI4 port into an
                on-chip ping-pong double-buffer, feed them to the gvsa_matmul
                language path. TILE_ELEMS=65536 (one gvsa operand set),
                N_TILES=16 (one language-step working set = 1 MB).

--- design ---
m_axi HBM read port (max_read_burst_length=256, num_read_outstanding=8).
Per tile: read_tile (burst RD into a stream) || feed_tile (drain to output),
inside a #pragma HLS DATAFLOW region so tile t+1's read overlaps tile t's
feed — the hls::stream IS the ping-pong double-buffer.
In the full system the TILE_LOOP would be gated by the 1 Hz language clock
enable (one working-set burst per language step); that gating is the caller's
concern — this IP executes the burst+feed when invoked.

